{
  "configuration_id": "config_044",
  "reason": "The strongest finding so far is that multiprofile dramatically improves RNA-only performance (scvi_n200: 0.52 single-profile → 0.65 multiprofile, a +0.13 gain), while aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) and fusion choice (weighted vs concat) show only marginal differences. No multimodal multiprofile configuration has been tested yet, leaving a critical uncertainty: does the multiprofile benefit transfer when an image modality is also present? config_044 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) directly tests this by combining the best-known RNA encoder (scvi_n200), image encoder (resnet50), aggregation (transformer, marginally better than avgpool), and fusion (weighted, marginally better than concat) in the multiprofile multimodal setting. It can be cleanly compared against config_027 (same encoders and fusion, single-profile) to isolate the multiprofile effect in the multimodal context. This is the highest-value next experiment because the multiprofile gain is the largest effect observed, and confirming or refuting its transfer to multimodal will determine the dominant design direction for all subsequent experiments."
}

